> [...]  Is there any way I can restore the game
> without having to see my systems administrator about it :-) ??

This really should be fixed in 3.1.

Everytime a character goes down (or up) the stairs, that character should
be saved to disk in a unique file. (Over-writting itself for each new
level, so there's only one character file per game.)

When the game starts, the game should search for existing level files,
and the character's file, and pick-up from there, (if the player so
desires.)

This is so similar to the current save-file routine, it shouldn't be hard
to implement.  And think of all the grief it would save from people who
suffer game-crashes...

